; output_charge_precedes_slot_bound: OUTPUT charges for the copy it makes
; before it validates the slot index, so a budget too small for the copy
; raises MemoryLimitExceeded even though the write would have been rejected
; as out of range anyway.
;
; spec/xqvm/SPEC.md's error-precedence rule orders an instruction as pops,
; then the charge, then type and range validation, and says in as many
; words that an instruction may raise MemoryLimitExceeded "for work it
; would never have done, because ... the index it was given is out of
; range". A VM that checked OutputIndex first would raise OUTPUT_INDEX
; here instead of MEMORY_LIMIT_EXCEEDED.
;
; Sizing, against the 1 GiB default so no vector-level budget is needed.
; A binary model of size n charges n * 8 to allocate and the same
; again for the copy OUTPUT makes, since its coefficient maps are empty.
; n = 100000000 charges 800000000 to allocate, which fits, and the copy
; would take the total to 1600000000, which does not. Slot 99 is outside
; the single output slot the run reserves.

PUSH 100000000
BQMX r0

PUSH 99
OUTPUT r0
HALT
